[{:db/id "q-141082/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "cf8f82be-8027-57f2-bd5a-4060f0575094" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141082/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "f544ad4c-287f-5f45-bf2b-4ef526b966c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141082/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "f4965f74-f800-520e-9e40-e0efcb2f4993" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141082/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ca1aaf8e-926d-59d2-8b66-4e1ff4215aa7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141082/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "eda4b349-f3ac-5703-b224-8300d536a6c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141082/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "140c983c-b009-5108-b1e0-38503d18bbf0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141082/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-141082/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-141082/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-141082/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-141082/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-141082/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141082" :question/id #uuid "90a72911-f2a4-5e18-9c98-33431b3777b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-141082" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{e}^{y}}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$\n- Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141082/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141082"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141080/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "30059b5a-4016-5fc7-8da6-22330210c414" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141080/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "d43b4b10-8063-5466-be3a-a3c3af6b66cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141080/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "e092af6a-ef57-5a2a-bda8-9a05223e717d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141080/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "c0f8d466-522b-5e38-8b40-10106f232e20" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141080/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "e002db91-eb89-5d8f-867f-e2b8d1fe3b76" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141080/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "44b7284a-24a3-59f0-acf0-ff9f993c64d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141080/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer-field/choices ["q-141080/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-141080/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-141080/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-141080/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-141080/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141080" :question/id #uuid "3c5d8fd2-fb66-5109-b8f5-6406e18d1fe6" :question/math-academy-id "q-141080" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$\n- Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\  & \\ne 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ and ${y}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}2y \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\ne \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141080/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141080"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141086/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "786090ba-9cbf-54ea-a394-9daafec6aad5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141086/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "f65988d8-7b63-5a3f-868e-57f1ee94e5fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141086/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "7dd0170d-f326-58f5-9749-6c0c86a31a6e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141086/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "91713830-f892-5573-a648-0a2929a227e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141086/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "b123aa26-72ff-5beb-b46d-3ca35327d703" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141086/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fd61664-dc80-5ee5-b6d5-ed8564b05673" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141086/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer-field/choices ["q-141086/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-141086/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-141086/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-141086/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-141086/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141086" :question/id #uuid "ca0e4ee1-6292-559e-9935-18a9adc4fe22" :question/math-academy-id "q-141086" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3y\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=3{e}^{-x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{-x}$\n- Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=3{e}^{-x},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(3{e}^{-x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{-x} \\\\  & \\ne 3{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=3{e}^{-x}$ and ${y}^{′}=-3{e}^{-x}$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}-3y \\\\ -3{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-3(3{e}^{-x}) \\\\ -3{e}^{-x} & \\ne -9{e}^{-x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=3{e}^{-x}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141086/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141086"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-140631"] :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)={x}^{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{5}.$\n- Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)={x}^{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{4})^{′} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3} \\\\  & \\ne 5{x}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y={x}^{4}$ and ${y}^{′}=4{x}^{3}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4y}{x} \\\\ (4{x}^{3}) & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4({x}^{4})}{x} \\\\ 4{x}^{3} & =4{x}^{3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y={x}^{4}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-141109/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "6a024b94-cda4-5d3b-941c-aaf7e25ae8de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141109/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ee5c774d-afee-57d7-84cf-a0112e0f4265" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141109/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "5a5bf16a-f239-598e-9644-b30e5b4ee7de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141109/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "acdc6c56-2315-55fb-9644-96753e024035" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141109/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "df57b554-74a6-5f0c-9daa-e52643a8a0cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141109/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d367f92-bd39-543c-a262-08c67e072c59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141109/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-141109/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-141109/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-141109/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-141109/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-141109/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141109" :question/id #uuid "7d075088-7ad8-5baf-a890-9be7b4897d61" :question/math-academy-id "q-141109" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2y,\\,y(0)=2.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{e}^{-2x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=A{e}^{-2x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(0)=2.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(0)=2$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{e}^{-2x} \\\\ 2 & =A{e}^{-2(0)} \\\\ 2 & =A{e}^{0} \\\\ 2 & =A(1) \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{-2x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141109/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141109"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352656/field-1/a1b2ccfba458a845fd8ee10e6daa31506496a50a50042e082232a7d8cf1de62a" :answer/id #uuid "5bc7ac89-5c15-5d25-b143-d16c7a705d16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352656/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "1f53f988-495a-5c39-b3eb-0c8f7fdbc467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352656/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "114bbd7e-95c4-5d24-8516-9822b36b1568" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352656/field-1/a1b2ccfba458a845fd8ee10e6daa31506496a50a50042e082232a7d8cf1de62a" :answer-field/choices ["q-352656/field-1/a1b2ccfba458a845fd8ee10e6daa31506496a50a50042e082232a7d8cf1de62a" "q-352656/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352656" :question/id #uuid "550459fd-d04d-5c33-8efe-cdcd1b67f25f" :question/math-academy-id "q-352656" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y,\\,y(-1)=4.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{e}^{x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=A{e}^{x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(-1)=4.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(-1)=4$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{e}^{x} \\\\ 4 & =A{e}^{-1} \\\\ 4 & =A{e}^{-1} \\\\ 4e & =A \\\\ A & =4e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352656/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352656"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141111/selection/4bd87ad5cdff0b2d0aa7574d5c7450ac33fa34774f895ce16d251ca09a1932ec" :answer/id #uuid "e9bb263f-9077-5675-9736-f53a031858a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141111/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "52a93f1f-33aa-5383-b49b-49