worked-solution "We're given that $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\sqrt{2}$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =A(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141111/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141111"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352655/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "4e9f9779-ffa0-5156-bb77-9064e661447e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281454 :answer-field/choices ["q-352655/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141108/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "27ce4f98-69c1-5501-9df2-126de889fad5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141108/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "da38b541-6ec6-5af7-b366-35bb89be2a83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141108/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "223e5c53-9d6a-57a8-acdb-78b763a3f1ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141108/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "ffd20074-d614-5913-957c-3e6b685ffdc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141108/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d496640d-5dc3-53d1-8063-49bf44149943" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141108/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "021c376f-b348-53b0-90c8-42e126191cbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141108/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-141108/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-141108/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-141108/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-141108/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-141108/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141108" :question/id #uuid "53021b4a-ecf6-51c5-9c2a-a4f9c53c3409" :question/math-academy-id "q-141108" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y,\\,y(0)=1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{e}^{-x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=A{e}^{-x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(0)=1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(0)=1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{e}^{-x} \\\\ 1 & =A{e}^{-0} \\\\ 1 & =A(1) \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=1{e}^{-x}={e}^{-x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141108/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141108"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
